 {
  "slug": "iceland-landscape-and-fashion",
  "title": "Iceland. Landscape and Fashion.",
  "date": "2019-09-20",
  "thumb": "4415",
  "group": "collaboration-projects",
  "tag": "Baiba Ladiga",
  "desc": "<p>Iceland -\nlunar fields, extraterrestrial colors, shadows of recent eruptions, silent ice\nand the raging Atlantic. Nature that will not leave anyone indifferent.\nSpontaneous winds and unique experience, impossible in any other place in\nEurope. </p>\n<p>Experience\nIceland through the endless panoramas, large strokes of nature and fashionable\nlooks. <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/smarts.studio/\">smArts.studio</a> presents our view of\nIceland, rhyming it's landscapes with designer dresses from Baiba Ladiga. The collaboration\nproject uncovers the fascinating nature of this country by incorporating fashion.\nAnd, of course, for this task it was impossible to find clothes more original\nthen <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/Ladigafashion/\">Baiba Ladiga’s\nconceptual fashion design</a>. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/smarts.studio/\">smArts.studio</a> - two people\nthat share common passion for photography, passion that has been developing for\ncombined more than 14 years, slowly growing from occasional shot of beautiful\nplace to something larger, to expressing ourselves. People that share so much\nof how we see the world that there is no need to speak or discus, we just\nshoot. Shoot to express our attitude, our dreams and our vision.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/Ladigafashion/\">Baiba Ladiga\n– Kobayashi (brand Baiba Ladiga)</a> is a conceptual designer based in Riga, Latvia. She studied at\nArt Academy Of Latvia and graduated in 2004. For five years she worked as\nfashion design lecturer in Shanghai as well did freelance design, styling and\nillustration projects. Three years ago ready to wear brand Baiba Ladiga was\nestablished. Mainly black and white, made of natural materials like wool, linen\nand cotton, inspired by architecture and minimalism. Brand focuses on\nsustainability and zero waste. And at the moment Baiba Ladiga collections are\nsold in EU and Japan and her avant-garde pieces are worn by style icons like\nLily Gatins.&nbsp;</p>",
  "blocks": [
